
==============================================================================
[2] the two failure modes respond differently
==============================================================================
  arm                                      median         failures > 5 %
  state mask + plume|test_id       0.7 ->   0.4 %           16 ->     4 %
  state mask + plume|test_ood      0.8 ->   0.8 %           36 ->    20 %
  state mask only|test_id         26.8 ->  19.1 %          100 ->    83 %

  With the plume, restarting removes 75 % of the in-distribution failures and 44 % of the
  out-of-distribution ones, because those were the optimiser losing an answer
  the data contained. The median reaches 0.4 %.

  With masks alone it moves the median from 26.8 % to 19.1 % and the p90 from 82 % to 41 %, and leaves 83 % of cases failing.
  8.6 % of that is the floor: the component of the starting
  error along the null direction, which no optimiser can see. The improvement
  it does make is the other five sixths of the perturbation being cleaned up,
  and it does not finish the job -- with masks only the misfit surface is
  nearly flat, so ranking three starts by misfit is a weak signal.

  The comparison that matters: 0.4 % with the plume against 19.1 % without, a factor of 46,
  with the mask-only arm unable to go below 8.6 % at any number of starts.
